' Authored by: Emmanuel A. Otchere (cardinal author rule, 2026-09-23)
'
' Agentic Workflow relational diagram
'
' Per CR-ES-006 §24 + ADR-ES-006 §22 + §26.
' Illustrates the 7 canonical relationships (specializes ;;; engages ;;;
' interprets ;;; operates-within ;;; coordinates ;; produces) plus the
' process-realized-through inverse.

@startuml agentic-workflow

skinparam backgroundColor #FFFFFF
skinparam defaultFontName Arial
skinparam defaultFontSize 10

skinparam rectangle {
    BackgroundColor #F0F8FF
    BorderColor #4682B4
}

title Agentic Workflow ;;; Relational Model

' Core Agentic Workflow class

rectangle "Agentic Workflow\n(ES:CONCEPT:agentic-workflow)" as awf #FFE4B5

' Specialization parent

rectangle "Workflow\n(ES:CONCEPT:workflow)" as wf #F0FFF0

' Subject types

rectangle "Process\n(external:concept:process)" as proc #E0E8F0

' Agent engagement

rectangle "Agent\n(ES:CONCEPT:agent)" as agent #F0E8FF

' Inherited semantics

rectangle "Intent\n(ES:CONCEPT:intent)" as intent #F5F5DC
rectangle "Authority\n(ES:CONCEPT:authority)" as auth #E0FFFF

' Coordinated entities

rectangle "Activity\n(external:concept:activity)" as activity #FFFACD
rectangle "Task\n(external:concept:task)" as task #FFFACD
rectangle "Outcome\n(external:concept:outcome)" as outcome #E0FFE0

' Relationships

awf --|> wf : specializes

proc --> awf : process-realized-through

awf --> agent : engages
awf --> intent : interprets
awf --> auth : operates-within

awf --> activity : coordinates
awf --> task : coordinates

awf --> outcome : produces

note bottom of awf
  Per CR-ES-006 §5 + ADR-ES-006 §2 + §18.
  Agentic Workflow specialises Workflow ;; preserves the Workflow
  semantics ;; adds 8 characteristics ;; 8 properties ;; 8 canonical
  relationships.
end note

note right of awf
  Per ADR-ES-006 §10 ;;; the material-participation criterion
  requires: "Agent interprets context ;; Agent selects permitted
  path ;; Workflow adapts".
end note

@enduml